    "text": "Abcán was a dwarf poet of the Tuatha De Danann, the early gods of Ireland. He appears in the story of Ruad, a goddess who gives her name to the falls of Assaroe. Ruad came from the Otherworld in Abcán's boat, which rode on a bronze hull and a tin sail. She did not live long here. She died at the falls, drawn by the song of a mermaid from his boat. In another tale Cuchulainn caught Abcán. Abcán sang so long that the hero slept. Abcán was kin to the dwarf musician Fer.",
